WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.567
-Looking good, bud.
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.667
Thank you for coming back.
Congratulations.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:08.234
You and your lovely wife, Claire
Danes, are expecting a baby.

00:00:08.234 --> 00:00:10.400
-What?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.133
-Am I right? [ Laughs ]

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:14.901
I'm surprising you. Yes.
-Wow, great.

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:17.601
-Surprise! Yeah, yeah.
That's fantastic.

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:18.868
-Yes, thank you.
-Third baby.

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:20.601
Are you ready for number three?
-No.

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:22.467
-No?
-No, no.

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:25.367
I mean, I'm very happy about it.
-Of course, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:26.901
But not prepared.
-But not ready.

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:28.667
Are you ever?
Are you ever ready?

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:32.100
-No.
-I personally feel like in

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.133
my limited experience that you
can only prepare as far as

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:37.801
the arrival of the baby and
everything after that is just --

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:40.000
just a blank.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.100
-How old are
your other two kids?

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.100
-10 and 4.
-Is that correct?

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.701
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah.
I had him when I was 8.

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:48.701
[ Laughter ]
-Exactly.

00:00:48.701 --> 00:00:51.000
Do they understand what Dad does
for a living or Mom?

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.534
-Uh.. [ Laughs ]

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:55.834
No, no. No, no, no. I was
thinking, do I understand?

00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:58.133
-Yeah, that's kind of -- Yeah.
I'm not sure if my kids know.

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:00.167
A little bit.
-They don't care.

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:02.701
-Yeah. Have you showed them
any of your movies?

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:04.534
-Well, there's not many that
would be...

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:05.834
-Appropriate.
-...appropriate.

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:08.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.200
I did show them
"Ella Enchanted."

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.367
I made one kids movie.

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:14.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.834
-That's a big deal.
-I know. It's a great film.

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:18.634
And people loved it
when they were kids.

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:20.167
And now, those people have
all grown up.

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:22.701
And that's kind of depressing
for me.

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:23.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:26.000
-Did your kids know it was you
in the movie?

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.100
-No. Well, the older one still
couldn't care less.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.567
And the younger one, we got
halfway through the movie,

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:33.400
and I was watching him.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.667
And eventually I said,
"You know, that's me.

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:37.300
That's Daddy in the movie."

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.801
He had no idea,
which was very sweet,

00:01:39.801 --> 00:01:41.701
which was maybe a testament
to my acting.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:42.968
Or not.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:44.834
-No, you were that
into the role.

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:46.200
Do they visit you on
"Law &amp; Order"?

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.767
-No, I was not that
into the role.

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:52.400
-You're like a method --
"That's not you, Dad."

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.033
-"Shut up, son."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:55.100
Take it in. Take it in.
-Daddy's speaking.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.100
Daddy has a monologue. Please.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.801
Do they go to "Law &amp; Order"?

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:00.868
-They have, yeah.
-They've been to the set?

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:03.234
-They've been to the set --
not to the iconic --

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:05.200
not to the offices and all that
stuff and the courtroom.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.734
But to the -- when we film, you
know, the courthouse steps,

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:09.968
which I guess is
kind of iconic --

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:11.667
-Of course.
-You know, come down the steps.

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:13.300
-Just to go root for Dad?

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.767
-No. Just because, honestly,
because we have Pop Tarts.

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:18.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:20.033
-They love Pop Tarts.

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:22.501
-It dawned on me like the fourth
time they came, yeah.

00:02:22.501 --> 00:02:25.167
-Yeah. You could just get
Pop Tarts for your house.

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:27.534
[ Laughter ]
-I could. I could.

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:29.100
But then they wouldn't come
to visit me at work.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:33.067
-Before we talk "Law &amp; Order,"

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:34.567
the Oscar nominations
just came out.

00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:36.734
And you were telling me that you
have a pretty personal

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:38.067
connection to one
of the nominees.

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:40.367
-I do. One of the front runners,
I think.

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:42.901
Yeah, it's an odd story.

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:44.367
-No, I love this story.
Please tell it.

00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:45.934
-So, this was several years ago.

00:02:45.934 --> 00:02:48.000
I was getting a wig made,
as you do.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.834
For professional purposes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:52.834
And the guy, you know,

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:55.167
they wrap your head in, like,
plastic wrap.

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:56.334
It's a whole process.

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:57.801
Anyway, he said,
"I don't know if

00:02:57.801 --> 00:02:59.767
I'm going to do this in time."
He called me back the next day

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:01.901
and said, "Good news.

00:03:01.901 --> 00:03:06.100
Your head is exactly the same
shape and size as somebody else

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.901
that I have worked on,
another actor.

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.868
And I have the mold of
their head at home.

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:11.000
So this is going to be a cinch
for me."

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.501
And I said, "Who's that?"

00:03:12.501 --> 00:03:14.000
And, you know, you're probably
thinking

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.033
it's Brendan Fraser or whatever.

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:16.400
But it's Cate Blanchett.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:23.267
-Cate Blanchett has your same
size head.

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:26.067
That's fantastic.
-It bodes well for me.

00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:28.567
-Are you honored? I mean, that's
so good, both of you guys.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.767
She should be honored as well.
Oh, my God.

00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:33.000
I never see both of you in
the same room at the same time.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:36.434
That's wild to know that you
have the same size head --

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:38.734
-It's very weird.
-Yeah, that's so --

00:03:38.734 --> 00:03:40.467
Alright.
Let's get into "Law &amp; Order."

00:03:40.467 --> 00:03:42.300
This is a big deal.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.167
Did you ever think you were
going to be this New York?

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:46.634
-No, I didn't, and I've lived
here for 15 years.

00:03:46.634 --> 00:03:48.033
And I still didn't feel entitled
to that.

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:50.334
-It's iconic, "Law &amp; Order."
-Yeah.

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:51.667
-It's very, very New York.

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:54.033
In fact, we found out you're not
the first family member

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.968
to act on "Law &amp; Order."
-Mm.

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:58.267
-Your wife, Claire Danes,
this was her TV debut.

00:03:58.267 --> 00:04:00.367
-Yeah.
-1992.

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:01.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:03.567
Isn't that odd?

00:04:03.567 --> 00:04:05.334
That was her first --
Now you're in it.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:07.667
-It's so strange, isn't it?
-It's got to be strange.

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:11.968
-Yeah. But then again, it's not
because, you know, every actor,

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:14.100
every New York actor that I'm
sure that comes through here

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.801
or that you see on Broadway
or whatever

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:17.334
has been on "Law &amp; Order."
-That's correct.

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:20.200
-Literally every actor.
Some of them 18 times.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.400
-Yes.
-But it's great.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.234
-It's a lot of people's
first acting roles.

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:26.033
What was your first acting role?
-Some of us, it's their last.

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:27.434
-That's true.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:29.400
A lot of -- Yeah, exactly yeah.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.334
I would love to play a dead body
on "Law &amp; Order."

00:04:31.334 --> 00:04:32.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:33.968
I would love to.
-Please.

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:35.334
I think you'd be just right.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:37.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:40.834
-Thank you so much. Wow.

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:43.934
But you -- What was -- Do you
remember your first role?

00:04:43.934 --> 00:04:47.267
-My first role was in England
obviously.

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:48.501
Well, maybe not obviously.

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:51.267
It was on a show called
"Trial and Retribution,"

00:04:51.267 --> 00:04:54.367
which is like the Anglicized
version of "Law &amp; Order."

00:04:54.367 --> 00:04:56.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:58.000
-"Trial and Retribution."

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.501
That just sounds a little bit --
-Donk, donk.

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:03.334
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:04.934
That's the theme song?
-Yes.

00:05:04.934 --> 00:05:06.968
-Donk, donk. Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:09.968
It's that much better
than our "Law &amp; Order."

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:12.267
Can you tell everyone who you
play on "Law &amp; Order"?

00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:13.834
-I play Nolan Price.

00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:16.567
He's the assistant district
attorney...

00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:18.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:18.467 --> 00:05:21.834
-...under --
I'm in Sam Waterston's office.

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:24.100
He's my boss now. He's moved up.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:26.601
It's super cool.
-That's the best.

00:05:26.601 --> 00:05:28.567
Donk, donk. I'm never going to
forget that. That's funny.

00:05:28.567 --> 00:05:31.067
I want to show a clip. Here's
Hugh Dancy in "Law &amp; Order."

00:05:31.067 --> 00:05:32.467
Take a look at this.

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:34.133
-We had a deal.

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:36.100
-I changed my mind.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.934
-You signed a cooperation
agreement.

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:40.167
It's binding and enforceable.

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:41.934
-[ Scoffs ]

00:05:41.934 --> 00:05:43.601
-There will be consequences.

00:05:43.601 --> 00:05:44.901
Do you not understand that?

00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:47.767
-Max is willing to plead guilty,
reckless endangerment.

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:49.400
-That's not on the table
anymore.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:52.167
You don't seem to hear
what I'm saying.

00:05:52.167 --> 00:05:55.501
I will revoke your bail,
send you back to Rikers,

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:58.400
and move forward on a charge of
manslaughter.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:05:59.801
-They're just blowing smoke.

00:05:59.801 --> 00:06:01.968
-No, we're serious.

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:06.701
-Well, I'm sorry. I can't do it.

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:10.667
-Come on. Hugh Dancy, everybody!

00:06:10.667 --> 00:06:15.033
"Law &amp; Order" airs Thursdays
at 8:00 p.m. on NBC,

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:16.901
and it's available the next day
on Peacock.

00:06:16.901 --> 00:06:19.067
More "Tonight Show" after
the break. Stick around.

00:06:19.067 --> 00:06:20.133
Thank you, buddy.

